    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42096" root="وعب" body-key="w">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَعْبٌ</span></b>  A <i>wide</i> road. (K.) You say, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">طَرِيقٌ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَعْبٌ</span>: and the pl. is <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وِعَابٌ</span>. (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وِعَابٌ</span>
<i>Wide</i> places in a land. (K.) Correctly, it is pl.
of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَعْبٌ</span>; but in the Moajam [el-Buldán] it is
made a proper name of certain places. (TA.)

